[2.3K, 2.4K]

22
00:02:28,738 --> 00:02:29,838
[Turn Old Hangers into a Clothes Rack]

23
00:02:29,838 --> 00:02:32,238
[Captain Park on the Go]

24
00:02:32,238 --> 00:02:34,972
[1M Views, Captain Park on the Go]
Yes, crew. Hello, this is Captain Park.

25
00:02:34,972 --> 00:02:38,838
[Captain Park's Family Moves into a New Home]
Today, we've got some amazing news.

26
00:02:38,838 --> 00:02:40,372
Yes, thanks to all of you,

27
00:02:40,372 --> 00:02:43,505
we finally made it
out of our rooftop apartment.

28
00:02:44,438 --> 00:02:45,838
Thank you.

29
00:02:45,838 --> 00:02:47,438
What are you doing, honey?

30
00:02:47,438 --> 00:02:48,972
Shall we give our crew a deep bow?

31
00:02:48,972 --> 00:02:50,005
- Sounds good.
- Yeah.

32
00:02:50,005 --> 00:02:51,005
Everyone!

33
00:02:51,005 --> 00:02:53,038
- Thank you so much.
- We truly appreciate it.

34
00:02:53,038 --> 00:02:55,872
- Thank you.
- We'll keep working hard and live well.

35
00:02:55,872 --> 00:02:57,938
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

36
00:02:57,938 --> 00:02:59,838
- Thank you!
- Thank you, everyone!

37
00:02:59,838 --> 00:03:03,072
Yes, this is Captain Park, everyone.
I've got some great news today.

38
00:03:03,072 --> 00:03:05,638
This is our new home.

39
00:03:05,638 --> 00:03:07,072
It's a brand-new apartment.

40
00:03:07,072 --> 00:03:10,838
We've got views on both sides. A city view!

41
00:03:10,838 --> 00:03:12,338
Honey, why does a new apartment
smell so good?

42
00:03:12,338 --> 00:03:15,338
I love it. I love it. I love it.

43
00:03:15,338 --> 00:03:16,938
It's all thanks to you.

44
00:03:16,938 --> 00:03:19,372
Just like we announced earlier,

45
00:03:19,372 --> 00:03:21,472
we've finished remodeling our new kitchen.

46
00:03:21,472 --> 00:03:24,572
- Wow, it looks incredible.
- Isn't this metal panel really dazzling?

47
00:03:24,572 --> 00:03:26,005
Thank you all so much.

48
00:03:26,005 --> 00:03:27,705
It's all thanks to you!

49
00:03:27,705 --> 00:03:28,738
Your turn, honey.

50
00:03:28,738 --> 00:03:29,838
- Yes, everyone!
- Let's bow.

51
00:03:29,838 --> 00:03:34,038
- We owe it all to you.
- Thank you so much, everyone.

52
00:03:42,638 --> 00:03:44,472
Yeah, everyone! Captain Park here.

53
00:03:44,472 --> 00:03:46,172
As we previewed today,

54
00:03:46,172 --> 00:03:47,872
- for the first time to our crew members,
- I'm not going.

55
00:03:47,872 --> 00:03:51,405
here's the first look
at Captain Park's new home.

56
00:03:53,672 --> 00:03:55,538
Eun Bin, Ye Ji, what are you doing?

57
00:03:55,538 --> 00:03:56,972
Come bow to our viewers.

58
00:03:56,972 --> 00:03:59,572
Seriously? That's embarrassing.

59
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:02,638
Hello, I'm Cha Eun Bin!

60
00:04:02,638 --> 00:04:06,172
What's so embarrassing about it?
I'm doing it too, okay? Come on.

61
00:04:06,172 --> 00:04:07,772
Well, you should.

62
00:04:07,772 --> 00:04:10,405
Your biggest hit is Mom's YouTube channel.

63
00:04:11,638 --> 00:04:13,905
Why would my biggest work
be your mom's YouTube channel?

64
00:04:13,905 --> 00:04:16,738
I've got plenty of great work to my name.

65
00:04:16,738 --> 00:04:18,405
Be careful, be careful.

66
00:04:19,838 --> 00:04:23,138
This is all for your beloved mom, Ye Ji.

67
00:04:23,138 --> 00:04:24,638
What did I always tell you?

68
00:04:24,638 --> 00:04:27,472
If you love someone,
you'll do anything for them.

69
00:04:27,472 --> 00:04:29,105
That's what really makes someone cool.

70
00:04:29,105 --> 00:04:30,672
Okay, Ye Ji?

71
00:04:30,672 --> 00:04:32,838
Besides, let's be honest.

72
00:04:32,838 --> 00:04:38,005
We got this amazing house
thanks to your mom. Isn't that true?

73
00:04:38,005 --> 00:04:39,605
That's true.

74
00:04:40,272 --> 00:04:42,705
- I'm going crazy, seriously...
- What? What's wrong, honey?

75
00:04:42,705 --> 00:04:44,238
Why on earth am I crying?

76
00:04:44,238 --> 00:04:46,572
You're crying? You shouldn't be crying.

77
00:04:46,572 --> 00:04:49,538
Not on a happy day like this. Cheer up!

78
00:04:50,605 --> 00:04:52,372
Ugh, seriously...

79
00:04:52,372 --> 00:04:54,538
What's gotten into them?

80
00:04:57,305 --> 00:05:00,572
If you don't want us getting kicked out,
hurry up and bow.

81
00:05:00,572 --> 00:05:02,338
Come on, Ye Ji.

82
00:05:03,472 --> 00:05:05,572
Crew members, thank you so much.

83
00:05:05,572 --> 00:05:08,605
We'll make the most of this!

84
00:05:08,605 --> 00:05:10,605
- Bow.
- Thank you!

85
00:05:10,605 --> 00:05:12,438
- Thank you!
- Thank you.

86
00:05:16,072 --> 00:05:17,138
Cut!

87
00:05:17,138 --> 00:05:20,738
Great. Nice work, everyone.

88
00:05:20,738 --> 00:05:22,005
- Did we get everything?
- Good job.

89
00:05:22,005 --> 00:05:23,672
Good job!

90
00:05:55,372 --> 00:05:58,872
[Presented to "Captain Park on the Go"
for Passing 1,000,000 Subscribers, YouTube]

91
00:06:43,638 --> 00:06:49,205
[Episode 1, Cheating Husband A]

92
00:06:55,138 --> 00:06:57,038
Connecting to Ye Ji's phone.

93
00:06:57,038 --> 00:06:59,705
<i>Connecting Ye Ji's CarPlay.</i>

94
00:06:59,705 --> 00:07:00,938
[The Day Captain Park's Family Moves
into a Luxury Single-Family Home]

95
00:07:00,938 --> 00:07:01,938
[You're cool, Captain Park!
Huge congratulations!]

96
00:07:01,938 --> 00:07:03,738
[It's absolutely gorgeous.
Congratulations, Captain Park!]

97
00:07:03,738 --> 00:07:04,772
[8:49 Why does Ye Ji look so cool?
I almost fell for a middle schooler]

98
00:07:04,772 --> 00:07:05,805
[Wow, as expected of my role model.
Her fashion sense is insane]

99
00:07:05,805 --> 00:07:06,805
[As expected of Captain Park!
Congratulations!]

100
00:07:06,805 --> 00:07:08,605
[9:01 Watching Ye Ji's smile on repeat
for the 249,837th time]

101
00:07:08,605 --> 00:07:10,272
[I love Captain Park's family so much,
I wish I were Captain Park's daughter]

102
00:07:18,038 --> 00:07:20,005
Come on, let's go already.

103
00:07:20,005 --> 00:07:22,105
Your only daughter is going to be late
for her first day of school.

104
00:07:22,105 --> 00:07:24,105
Yeah, we've still got time.

105
00:07:24,105 --> 00:07:27,138
The girl in the house across from us
is in your school and grade.

106
00:07:27,138 --> 00:07:30,138
Wouldn't it be nice
to start off with a friend?

107
00:07:30,138 --> 00:07:33,572
Just because she's my age and lives
next door doesn't mean we'll be friends.

108
00:07:33,572 --> 00:07:35,405
Oh, there she is!

109
00:07:40,138 --> 00:07:41,905
Min Seo!

110
00:07:43,272 --> 00:07:46,772
Are you sure you don't want a ride?

111
00:07:47,472 --> 00:07:50,005
- Hello!
- Hello!

112
00:07:50,005 --> 00:07:52,572
- Oh, yeah.
- We moved into the house across the street.

113
00:07:52,572 --> 00:07:54,338
- Hello.
- Yeah.

114
00:07:54,338 --> 00:07:57,105
Oh, you go to
Cheongnam Girls' Middle School too?

115
00:07:57,105 --> 00:07:58,272
- Oh, hi.
- Perfect timing.

116
00:07:58,272 --> 00:08:01,105
We were just about to head to school.

117
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,205
Would you like a ride?

118
00:08:02,205 --> 00:08:04,838
We should save gas and save time
in a country that doesn't produce oil.

119
00:08:04,838 --> 00:08:07,105
And it's good for the girls
to become friends.

120
00:08:07,105 --> 00:08:08,672
Neighbors should help each other out.

121
00:08:08,672 --> 00:08:12,005
Thanks, but maybe not today.

122
00:08:12,005 --> 00:08:17,305
Oh, how about
having a meal together on the weekend?

123
00:08:17,305 --> 00:08:19,838
Just check with your husband and let us know.

124
00:08:19,838 --> 00:08:22,605
I'm actually a pretty good cook.

125
00:08:22,605 --> 00:08:24,205
Oh, okay.

126
00:08:24,205 --> 00:08:27,272
By the way, I guess your husband
left for work earlier.

127
00:08:31,738 --> 00:08:36,905
I never imagined someone
this famous would move in next door.

128
00:08:36,905 --> 00:08:41,005
I know. We never imagined we'd end up
living in this neighborhood either.

129
00:08:41,005 --> 00:08:43,605
It's all thanks to our Captain Park.

130
00:08:43,605 --> 00:08:45,738
I see you film all over
different neighborhoods.

131
00:08:45,738 --> 00:08:48,738
Oh? Have you seen our YouTube channel?

132
00:08:48,738 --> 00:08:51,005
Wait, are you one of our crew members
by any chance?

133
00:08:51,005 --> 00:08:53,172
You're not going to do that here too,
are you?

134
00:08:53,172 --> 00:08:56,638
I'm just not used to
all the noise and commotion.

135
00:08:58,172 --> 00:08:59,772
Wait.

136
00:09:00,772 --> 00:09:03,405
I stopped by yesterday to drop this off,
but no one was home.

137
00:09:03,405 --> 00:09:05,338
[Park Kyung Hee, CEO of the ZiP]
It's a housewarming rice cake.

138
00:09:06,905 --> 00:09:09,172
You really went through a lot of trouble.

139
00:09:09,172 --> 00:09:12,038
People around here
don't usually do this kind of thing.

140
00:09:12,038 --> 00:09:14,972
You don't have to go to
all this trouble next time.

141
00:09:14,972 --> 00:09:16,672
Not at all.

142
00:09:18,472 --> 00:09:21,805
Sometimes too much thoughtfulness
can be a bit overwhelming.

143
00:09:23,072 --> 00:09:25,172
Min Seo, get in the car.

144
00:09:25,172 --> 00:09:27,505
Thank you for the ride.

145
00:09:33,905 --> 00:09:36,438
Wow. That's insane.

146
00:09:36,438 --> 00:09:39,438
What a load of crap, seriously.

147
00:09:39,438 --> 00:09:42,638
That's why her own daughter
openly ignores her.

148
00:09:42,638 --> 00:09:46,238
"Sometimes too much thoughtfulness
can be a bit overwhelming."

149
00:09:46,238 --> 00:09:48,738
What a two-faced punk.

150
00:09:48,738 --> 00:09:50,838
Who does she think she is,
treating someone's kindness like garbage?

151
00:09:50,838 --> 00:09:52,038
That's what I'm saying.

152
00:09:52,038 --> 00:09:54,538
Honey, here. Pull.

153
00:09:55,338 --> 00:09:56,538
So, Hong.

154
00:09:56,538 --> 00:09:59,338
Please stop wasting money on ugly brown cars
and start moving in better circles.

155
00:09:59,338 --> 00:10:04,505
That's the only way
people will stop looking down on you.

156
00:10:05,305 --> 00:10:09,738
Honey, just the wrap on that car
cost five million won.

157
00:10:09,738 --> 00:10:12,538
And it's not brown. It's called "Rich Gold."

158
00:10:12,538 --> 00:10:14,738
What do you mean by "Rich Gold"?

159
00:10:14,738 --> 00:10:16,472
Is that some kind of pizza?

160
00:10:17,538 --> 00:10:20,072
She's definitely got a personality disorder.

161
00:10:20,072 --> 00:10:22,972
Otherwise, she's the daughter
of Cheongnam Hospital, a doctor,

162
00:10:22,972 --> 00:10:26,705
elegant, well... pretty, and classy.

163
00:10:26,705 --> 00:10:30,372
She's got everything,
yet her husband still left her.

164
00:10:30,372 --> 00:10:33,372
But I heard they ran the hospital together
and got along well.

165
00:10:33,372 --> 00:10:36,238
So that real estate agent
lied to us back then?

166
00:10:36,238 --> 00:10:38,505
Yeah, apparently it was all a lie.

167
00:10:38,505 --> 00:10:40,805
I could tell just by the way
that woman acted.

168
00:10:40,805 --> 00:10:43,172
So I grilled the real estate agent,

169
00:10:43,172 --> 00:10:44,972
and it turns out her husband

170
00:10:44,972 --> 00:10:48,472
abandoned the house, the hospital,
everything, and ran off.

171
00:10:48,472 --> 00:10:50,472
Apparently, the woman next door

172
00:10:50,472 --> 00:10:51,938
came running out barefoot,

173
00:10:51,938 --> 00:10:55,405
sobbing and grabbing his legs,
causing a huge scene.

174
00:10:56,472 --> 00:10:58,505
She acted so refined and classy,

175
00:10:58,505 --> 00:11:01,872
but turns out she's a total mess.

176
00:11:02,738 --> 00:11:06,638
Anyway, they've been
separated for months now.

177
00:11:08,172 --> 00:11:09,205
[Ryu Ji Su: Thank you, oppa
Me: See you next time]

178
00:11:09,205 --> 00:11:11,772
[We'll finally see each other tomorrow]
No wonder she looked so miserable.

179
00:11:11,772 --> 00:11:13,972
What are you talking about?

180
00:11:13,972 --> 00:11:16,605
But why on earth is that woman like that?

181
00:11:16,605 --> 00:11:19,605
Honey, ignore her! Just ignore her.

182
00:11:19,605 --> 00:11:22,472
Neighbors being close?
Please. Don't bother with that nonsense.

183
00:11:22,472 --> 00:11:23,972
Like that's even a thing.

184
00:11:23,972 --> 00:11:28,505
From now on, even if she begs
to be friends, I'm done with her.

185
00:11:28,505 --> 00:11:33,472
So, Hong, just completely
ignore her from now on.

186
00:11:33,472 --> 00:11:36,938
Okay, I'm not even going to
say hello to her anymore.

187
00:11:36,938 --> 00:11:39,738
Even if she greets me first,
I'll pretend I didn't see her.

188
00:11:42,405 --> 00:11:45,305
But does the IR deck
really need this much text?

189
00:11:45,305 --> 00:11:47,272
Yes, then I'll reorganize it
and send it over again.

190
00:11:47,272 --> 00:11:49,638
It's the DIY paint prototype samples
you mentioned before.

191
00:11:49,638 --> 00:11:51,138
Yes, number two.

192
00:11:51,138 --> 00:11:53,572
But the actual color
looks completely different.

193
00:11:53,572 --> 00:11:56,038
Check whether it's an issue with the product
or the display and let me know.

194
00:11:56,038 --> 00:11:57,038
Yes.

195
00:11:57,038 --> 00:11:59,772
- And here's the final thumbnail version.
- Yeah.

196
00:12:00,872 --> 00:12:02,738
Oh, it's too cluttered.

197
00:12:02,738 --> 00:12:06,138
Use version three as the base
and remove anything unnecessary.

198
00:12:06,138 --> 00:12:08,938
- This will be our first impression.
- Yes, I'll update it right away.

199
00:12:08,938 --> 00:12:12,105
This is the product
that will be featured in this episode.

200
00:12:12,105 --> 00:12:16,238
We're planning to highlight that
it's waterproof, resistant to stains,

201
00:12:16,238 --> 00:12:18,138
- and highly breathable.
- It's soft.

202
00:12:18,138 --> 00:12:21,872
Yes, since it's popular among families
with children and pets,

203
00:12:21,872 --> 00:12:23,272
we're thinking of
adding that concept as well.

204
00:12:23,272 --> 00:12:25,405
- Yes, sounds good.
- Captain Park!

205
00:12:25,405 --> 00:12:27,738
Just a moment, just a moment.

206
00:12:28,572 --> 00:12:31,838
Info on Michelle Jung's associates!

207
00:12:32,738 --> 00:12:34,472
[Michelle Jung, provides support
and investments across various fields]

208
00:12:34,472 --> 00:12:36,672
[Director Ahn Won Seok of Cheongnam General]
I had a really hard time.

209
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:37,833
[CEO Park Kyung Hee]
These days, even Korea doesn't invest

210
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:40,205
based on connections.

211
00:12:40,205 --> 00:12:42,738
She's only Michelle in name.

212
00:12:42,738 --> 00:12:48,138
Her mindset is completely stuck
in the past, like she never left Korea.

213
00:12:48,138 --> 00:12:49,972
I can't stand it, seriously.

214
00:12:51,305 --> 00:12:55,172
Anyway, look into it. See if there's
anyone we can get an introduction to.

215
00:12:55,172 --> 00:12:58,405
Director Kwak,
you must've worked your tail off.

216
00:12:58,405 --> 00:13:02,305
Still, even if it means dealing with this,
we need Michelle Jung's investment.

217
00:13:02,305 --> 00:13:05,272
Her name alone will make
future investments easier to secure.

218
00:13:05,272 --> 00:13:08,472
[Director Joo Bo Sung, CEO Kim Ji Yeon]
We need investment to expand the business,

219
00:13:08,472 --> 00:13:11,172
pay our employees,

220
00:13:11,172 --> 00:13:13,605
and finally ease some of the pressure.

221
00:13:18,705 --> 00:13:20,672
This is driving me crazy, seriously.

222
00:13:20,672 --> 00:13:22,473
[Director Ahn Soo Jung, Dermatologist,
Her father's connection with Michelle Jung]

223
00:13:22,473 --> 00:13:24,205
[led her to volunteer with her often]

224
00:13:24,205 --> 00:13:26,105
A billion won? Ten billion won?

225
00:13:26,105 --> 00:13:27,705
Don't do this.

226
00:13:27,705 --> 00:13:30,672
If money was what I cared about,
I would have never dated you, Ji Hoon.

227
00:13:31,905 --> 00:13:34,438
I'll siphon off hundreds of millions,
even billions,

228
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:38,538
from Han Jung Woo's townhouse
and bring it to you, Ji Hoon.

229
00:13:38,538 --> 00:13:40,905
But that's as far as you can go.

230
00:13:40,905 --> 00:13:44,505
You can't be Ji Yeon's father.

231
00:13:44,505 --> 00:13:46,205
Cut!

232
00:13:47,105 --> 00:13:48,438
Yes, okay!

233
00:13:48,438 --> 00:13:51,005
Director, was my acting okay?

234
00:13:51,005 --> 00:13:53,305
Yes, Ms. Ryu! That was great.

235
00:13:53,305 --> 00:13:55,605
I almost cried, seriously.

236
00:13:57,572 --> 00:14:01,738
Wow, idols these days
are all pretty good actors,

237
00:14:01,738 --> 00:14:04,638
but how is she so consistently bad?

238
00:14:04,638 --> 00:14:08,272
If she could act well too,
she'd be a world star by now.

239
00:14:08,272 --> 00:14:10,372
Mr. Kang, please teach her a bit.

240
00:14:10,372 --> 00:14:12,572
When it comes to acting,
who else but Kang Tae Han?

241
